# Everything under docs/ is ignored and each tracked surface is re-included by name, so a new
# scaffolding directory is ignored by default and a new tracked doc is a deliberate line — the
# inverse of naming each stale directory individually and missing the next one.
# Audit reports are one-run records of this repo on one machine: written locally, never shipped to
# installers — the `local` cell in every column of references/config.md § Doc tracking, which owns
# that call. docs/audits/ is re-included so the directory is visible and docs/audits/* keeps its
# contents out of every commit. The v0.12 disposition register is a closure ledger
# docs/decisions/README.md cites, so it is the one exception.
docs/*
!docs/*.md
!docs/comparisons/
!docs/devcycle/
!docs/audits/
!docs/case-studies/
!docs/design/
!docs/decisions/
!docs/configuration/
!docs/pipeline/
!docs/playbooks/
docs/audits/*
!docs/audits/2026-08-06-disposition-register.md
# Routing advisories are one-run records of this repo's own dispatch costs: written locally, never
# shipped to installers. Other repos do commit their copy — that is the `commit` cell in
# references/config.md § Doc tracking, which already scopes every such cell to what the host repo's
# own ignore rules allow, and this repo's answer is no.
docs/devcycle/routing-advisories.md
